---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
	title="Privacy"
	description="What malikstefan.com and Report Harmonizer collect, why, who else handles it, and how to have it deleted."
>
	<article>
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="meta">
			Last updated <time datetime="2026-11-09">November 9, 2026</time>
		</p>

		<p>
			This page explains what I collect on malikstefan.com and in Report Harmonizer at
			app.malikstefan.com, why I collect it, and who else handles it.
		</p>

		<h2>Who I am</h2>
		<p>
			I'm Malik Machaieie. I run this site and Report Harmonizer on my own, from Denmark, and I'm
			responsible for your data. If you have a question about anything on this page, email me at
			<a href="mailto:contact@malikstefan.com">contact@malikstefan.com</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>I don't show ads.</li>
			<li>I don't sell your data.</li>
			<li>Analytics only run if you say yes.</li>
			<li>
				You can ask to see or delete your data at any time, and I'll handle it within 3 business
				days.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>This website</h2>

		<h3>Analytics</h3>
		<p>
			I use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages bring visitors and sign-ups. It only loads after
			you click Accept on the cookie banner. If you decline, no analytics cookies are set.
		</p>
		<p>If you accept, Google Analytics collects:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>the pages you view</li>
			<li>the site that sent you here</li>
			<li>your approximate location, worked out from your IP address</li>
			<li>your device type</li>
			<li>a visitor ID stored in a cookie</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			You can change your choice at any time with the Cookie settings link in the footer. You can
			also block cookies in your browser.
		</p>
		<p>Analytics data is kept for 2 months.</p>

		<h3>Email list</h3>
		<p>
			If you sign up for emails, I store your email address and the date you confirmed. Nothing
			else. The list is stored with Buttondown, which also sends the emails.
		</p>
		<p>
			Sign-up is double opt-in. After you enter your address, you get an email asking you to
			confirm, and I don't send anything until you do.
		</p>
		<p>
			I send occasional emails about Report Harmonizer, a few a month. Every email has an
			unsubscribe link. If you unsubscribe, I stop emailing you. If you also want your address
			deleted from the list, email me.
		</p>

		<h2>Report Harmonizer</h2>

		<h3>Signing in</h3>
		<p>
			You sign in with a link sent to your email address. These emails are sent with Resend. I
			store your email address and your sign-in sessions. A session stores a session token, its
			expiry time, your IP address and your browser type. The session token is kept in a sign-in
			cookie, which the app needs to work.
		</p>

		<h3>Your reports</h3>
		<p>When you use Report Harmonizer, I store:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>the Word reports you upload</li>
			<li>the edited files the app produces</li>
			<li>the style rules you set</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			These are stored on my server at DigitalOcean in New York, USA. I keep them until you ask me
			to delete them.
		</p>

		<h3>AI editing</h3>
		<p>
			To make the edits, the app sends the text of your report and your style rules to Anthropic
			through the Claude API. You can read how Anthropic handles data in
			<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic's privacy policy</a>.
		</p>

		<h3>Payments</h3>
		<p>
			Payments are handled by Stripe. I never see your card number. I store your Stripe customer
			ID and your subscription status.
		</p>

		<h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Service</th>
					<th scope="col">What for</th>
					<th scope="col">Where</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td>Google Analytics</td>
					<td>Website analytics, only if you accept</td>
					<td>USA</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Buttondown</td>
					<td>Email list</td>
					<td>USA</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Resend</td>
					<td>Sign-in emails</td>
					<td>USA</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>DigitalOcean</td>
					<td>Stores app files</td>
					<td>New York, USA</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Anthropic</td>
					<td>AI editing of report text</td>
					<td>USA</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Stripe</td>
					<td>Payments</td>
					<td>Ireland and USA</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			Some of these companies are in the USA. They each describe in their own privacy policy how
			they protect data transferred from the EU.
		</p>

		<h2>Why I'm allowed to use your data</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Analytics and the email list: your consent.</li>
			<li>Report Harmonizer: the contract between us when you use the app.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>You can ask me to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>show you the data I have about you</li>
			<li>correct it</li>
			<li>delete it</li>
			<li>export it</li>
			<li>stop using it, if you object</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Email <a href="mailto:contact@malikstefan.com">contact@malikstefan.com</a> and I'll handle
			your request within 3 business days.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you're in the EU and unhappy with how I handle your data, you can complain to
			<a href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk">Datatilsynet</a>, the Danish data protection authority.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	.meta {
		margin: 0 0 2rem;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
		font-family: var(--sans);
	}
</style>
